# Deployment configuration for slackline-timer.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.deploy` (git-ignored) and fill in your own values.
# Nothing here is secret in the cryptographic sense — no keys, no tokens — but
# it is operator- and account-specific, so it is deliberately not committed.
#
# Loaded automatically by every piece of deploy/ops tooling: `server/infra/app.ts`
# (the CDK entrypoint), `web/internals/deployToS3.mjs` (the frontend deploy),
# `server/scripts/lib/awsCli.mjs` (commission / decommission / maintenance) and
# `server/scripts/cognito/cognitoCommon.mjs` (the Cognito helpers). An
# already-exported variable still wins. Real secrets live in SSM SecureString
# parameters and are fetched at runtime — never here.

# The AWS CLI profile used for `cdk deploy` and the S3/CloudFront sync.
AWS_PROFILE=<your-profile>

# The AWS account the stacks live in — the one value of this file that every
# tool needs and that is nowhere in the committed tree. The account actually
# deployed to resolves from the credentials above; `server/infra/app.ts` fails
# the synth when the two disagree, so this catches a wrong-profile deploy before
# CloudFormation runs. It also names the environment `cdk gc` collects
# (`scripts/maintenance/gcBootstrapAssets.mjs`, via resolveAccount()) and the
# account the Cognito helpers blame in their wrong-account diagnosis.
AWS_ACCOUNT_ID=<account-id>

# The address subscribed to the cost backstop (ADR 0031 §1): the monthly AWS
# Budget's 50/80/100% notifications and the us-east-1 EstimatedCharges alarm.
# REQUIRED to deploy the billing stack — it fails fast rather than subscribe a
# dead address and silently turn the cost guardrail into a no-op. Prefer a
# distribution list over an individual mailbox.
BILLING_ALERT_EMAIL=<billing-alert-email>
